  "description": "The racing alternative to our classic SILEX 9000, combining proven SILEX traits, like tyre clearance, geometry and handling, with some additional aero features to get the SILEX RS 9000 ready for your next long-distance gravel race.\n\nThe SILEX already has a successful racing pedigree, but the world of gravel racing is constantly evolving. Our SILEX RS 9000 is the next step in SILEX's evolution. In addition to the typical SILEX attributes, the aero-optimised, gravel-specific Sharq GR wheelset from Fulcrum with a 30 mm rim bed creates maximum tyre volume for comfort and control while reducing drag. Meanwhile, the Vision aero one-piece cockpit and Rotor cranks with an aero chainring also contribute to making the SILEX RS 9000 the most race-ready SILEX to date.\n\nAdventure and racing - all combined in one proven package. To give riders the option to rely on the proven SILEX concept when the racing urge kicks in, we have created the new SILEX RS. Adopting the key principles of the SILEX, of a sporty yet comfortable geometry that keeps the bike stable even after multiple hours in the saddle, ample tyre clearance to deal with the most demanding of courses and multiple fixing points to securely attach equipment and nutrition storage compartments, the RS range goes one step further to get the SILEX race-ready. A proven one-piece aero cockpit and specific aero chainring give it the aero touch, while the aero-optimised gravel-specific wheelset with an extra-wide rim bed helps get the maximum out of the tyres in terms of grip and comfort, while also contributing to the aero credentials of the SILEX RS. If our MISSION is too aggressive and our standard SILEX too adventure-focused, then the SILEX RS delivers the perfect combination of aerodynamic, tyre clearance and long-distance geometry.",
